      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\frac{5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x){e}^{x}-(5-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x){e}^{x}}{({e}^{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-5+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-5}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
